The '''Dark Room''' is one of five final levels in ''The Binding of Isaac: Rebirth'', alongside the {{s|Chest}}, {{s|The Void}}, the {{s|Corpse}}, and {{s|Home}}. The Dark Room is unlocked by defeating {{e|Satan}} 5 times, after which it can be accessed by touching the chest dropped by Satan with {{i|The Negative}} equipped. Entrance to the Dark Room can also be achieved via the {{r|I AM ERROR}} room in {{s|Sheol}}, even without {{i|The Negative}}, as well as through the {{r|Black Market}} in Sheol, and through a trapdoor spawned by a button. After completing this level or the Chest for the first time, the Dark Room will always contain a large golden door in the first room, which can be unlocked with either the Key Pieces (combination of {{i|Key Piece 1}} and {{i|Key Piece 2}}), {{i|Dad's Key}}, {{p|Get out of Jail Free Card}}, or {{i|Mr. ME!}}.

{{dlc|a}} The Dark Room can also be accessed by repeatedly using a {{r|Sacrifice Room}}. After using the spikes for the 12th time, continuing to use the Sacrifice Room will have a 50% chance to teleport Isaac directly to the Dark Room, regardless of what floor he was previously on.

{{dlc+|a+}} The Dark Room is home to the [[Grave Room]], which will contain a [[Dirt Patch]], which can be dug up using {{i|Mom's Shovel}}. Doing so for the first time will unlock {{C|The Forgotten}}. On subsequent runs, multiple Dirt Patches can be found, and digging them up using {{i|We Need To Go Deeper!}}, {{p|Ehwaz}}, or Mom's Shovel will spawn a random type of [[chest]].{{dlc-}}

Like {{s|Sheol}} before it, the Dark Room consists of only one floor. In the Dark Room, it is not possible to bomb doors open to skip rooms. The Dark Room's rooms are usually devoid of [[Rocks]] and other obstacles; but are mainly filled with [[boss]]es and [[mini-boss]]es. The boss of the floor is always {{e|The Lamb}}.

The first room the player spawn in will automatically contain 4 {{e|Red Chest}}s that {{Dlc|nr}}function normally or {{Dlc|r}}contain random [[Devil Room (Item Pool)|Devil Deals]]. Rerolling these items will produce new items that are from the [[Treasure Room (Item Pool)|Treasure Room item pool]]. As well, all other types of chests spawned in the Dark Room will always contain Treasure Room items. {{Dlc|nr}}Destroying {{machine|Slot Machine}}s, {{machine|Fortune Telling Machine}}s, and all types of {{machine|Beggar}}s with the exception of {{machine|Shell Game}} will also spawn items.

